  "id": "COMPOUND:16888 - PROTEIN:4709",
  "verbalization": "Theasaponin E1 is shown to have multiple targets, including TAO1, Carboxypeptidase D, and Placenta growth factor, all of which are targets of K-252a. K-252a is a known inhibitor of MAP/microtubule affinity-regulating kinase 4, suggesting a potential mechanism of action through the inhibition of this kinase. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Theasaponin E1 and the target kinase, with K-252a acting as a bridge in each case. The shared target of K-252a suggests that the mechanism of action may involve the inhibition of a common downstream pathway, possibly through the modulation of microtubule dynamics or other cellular processes regulated by this kinase. The presence of multiple targets and the consistent scores across different paths support a robust mechanistic link between Theasaponin E1 and MAP/microtubule affinity-regulating kinase 4, with K-252a serving as a critical mediator in this relationship.",
